Hey, {VAR 0100 0000}.{VAR BE01}
Have you come looking for the
Gym Leader?

He was here talking about Pokémon
types until just a few moments ago...{VAR BE01}
Maybe you walked right past him?{VAR BE01}

Nothing improves your skill as a Trainer
like real battles.{VAR BE01}
That's why challenging Gym Leaders is
great practice.{VAR BE01}

Really? I really want to try out my
items, so I'll just wait here until you{VAR BE00}
decide you're ready.

Cheren: Well, let's see how effective
my items are...{VAR BE01}
Or maybe I should test how well I can
battle without items...?{VAR BE01}
Anyway, this is an indoor match, so let's
battle without getting too rough!{VAR BE01}

Cheren: So learning to use items well is
definitely important, then.{VAR BE01}
Oh, here. {VAR 0100 0000}, I'll give you
these Berries.{VAR BE01}

Cheren: If you give a Pokémon this kind
of Berry to hold, it will eat it to heal up{VAR BE00}
when its HP goes down in battle.{VAR BE01}
But if you give Pokémon man-made items
like Potions to hold, they can't{VAR BE00}
use them.{VAR BE01}
Well, good luck, then.{VAR BE01}

This Trainers' School exists to meet the
demands of Trainers who want to know{VAR BE00}
more about Pokémon because they{VAR BE00}
love them!

Pokémon have mysterious powers
called Abilities.{VAR BE01}
Abilities have a variety of effects, and
many of those effects are activated when{VAR BE00}
Pokémon are in battle!

There is a technique that lets you
cancel evolution!{VAR BE01}
I'll read the book about it to you.
Are you ready?{VAR BE01}
“You can surprise a Pokémon and stop its
evolution by pressing the B Button when{VAR BE00}
a Pokémon is evolving."

Some moves can only be taught with TMs.{VAR BE01}
TMs can be used over and over, so you
might want to use them a lot.{VAR BE01}
If you don't like the move you taught,
you can always use a different TM.

So here is the question:{VAR BE01}
Which of the following items
cures poison?

Ding ding ding!{VAR BE01}
Right answer!
Now for the next question.{VAR BE01}

Ding ding ding! We have a winner!
Fantastic answer!{VAR BE01}
Since you know so much about status
conditions, I'll give you this!{VAR BE01}

Buzzzzz!{VAR BE01}
Too bad... That's incorrect.
Please try again sometime!

If poisoned, a Pokémon steadily loses HP
when battling.{VAR BE01}
The poison lingers after the battle.
To cure it, use an Antidote.{VAR BE01}

Paralysis reduces the Speed stat
and may prevent movement.{VAR BE01}
It remains after battle, so use a
Parlyz Heal.{VAR BE01}

If a Pokémon falls asleep, it will be
unable to attack.{VAR BE01}
The Pokémon may wake up on its own,
but if a battle ends while it is{VAR BE00}
sleeping, it will stay asleep.{VAR BE01}
Wake it up using an Awakening.{VAR BE01}

A burn reduces the Attack stat and
steadily reduces the victim's HP.{VAR BE01}
A burn lingers after battle.
Cure a burn using a Burn Heal.{VAR BE01}

If a Pokémon is frozen, it becomes
completely helpless.{VAR BE01}
The Pokémon may thaw out on its own,
but if a battle ends while it is{VAR BE00}
frozen, it will stay frozen.{VAR BE01}
Thaw it out using an Ice Heal.{VAR BE01}
